Z||000000||WisconsinGT||02-12-2000||11:17 PM||||I just picked one up today. I know, I should get the MSD, Jacobs ignition. But putting another 0 after the $50.00 I paid for the Accel is not an option at this time. Anyway, after looking at the coil I have now, (stock)  I noticed that they both look similar. But I do not know what I need to take apart. Can someone give me the lowdown on this mod.? <BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||TOM||02-12-2000||11:38 PM||||msd coils are $36||||reg||1
Z||000002||WisconsinGT||02-12-2000||11:51 PM||||Damn Tom, If I only knew. I guess I can take the Accel  coil back. This brings up another point... Is one better then the other?  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||02-13-2000||09:49 AM||||I bought the Accel coil along with Accel super stock spiral wound 8mm wires and Bosch Platinum plugs.  I don't know for sure, bt I think if you have a weak link; i.e. cheap wires, plugs, then you may not see much improvement.  As far as comparing the 2, never tried it. I can pretty much guarantee that the shop will not return it for refund due to being electronic parts. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||TOM||02-13-2000||12:25 PM||||They are probably the same in quality. I too dont thin they will return it if it is opened.||||reg||1
Z||000005||WisconsinGT||02-13-2000||12:49 PM||||Stimpy,<P>Can you tell me what I need to do in order to install the coil? i.e. Do I need to remove anything? Do I need to cut/grind anything? Do I need to reset the timing after the install?<P>I have new wires, cap, plugs, I am looking for a little improvement as far as my car missing at idle. I know the electronics are usually the first to go. Looking at the coil I have now, it looks old and original. So I think it is a good thing to do at this juncture. Plus, at 79,000 miles...I am thinking 3.4 swap might be a reality if I cannot get tis engine to perform like it should. <BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||02-13-2000||01:15 PM||||The coil I have looks just like the factory coil, exceot it has yellow casing. It hooks up just like the factory coil, just remove the 2 bolts holding the coil mounting bracket to the base, remove the 2 nuts and bolts holding the coil to the bracket and do the opposite with the new coil. Easy money. Did someone sell you one of those big whomper Accel super coils (universal application)?  I don't think one of those wil work as it does not have the plug in connectors.  If someone sold you the wrong application, go get the right one and save yourself a headache. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||WisconsinGT||02-14-2000||11:45 PM||||Thanks Stimpy! I have the same Accel coil you have. But after taking off my coil, I noticed that I have riviots holding my coil to the mounting brace. That sucks. Oh well!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||TOM||02-15-2000||12:07 AM||||That must still be the original from pontiac. You need to drill or grind the rivets off and replace with screws and nuts.||||reg||1
